-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth), first reading print (Senate),
-- 7 September 2026 (file 26S2721).
-- Part 2 -- Selection process for diplomatic appointments -- main provisions (ss 9-11).
--
-- Imports Part 3 (the Selection Committee, ss 12-13), which imports Part 1 (ss 1-8).

IMPORT `part3-committees`

§ `Appointments and acting arrangements`

-- An appointment to an office, with what ss 9, 10, 14 and 15 ask about it. The Bill does not say
-- who appoints (REF-17): the appointing act and whether the Governor-General made it are facts.
-- `Selection Committees for the office` lists every Committee established for an appointment to
-- the office, earlier vacancies included, in the order they were established; FORK-04 decides
-- which of them s 9(3) and s 10(6) count. `the previous appointment to the office was made on`
-- is the day the last appointment to the office was made before this one (a day before any
-- Committee in the list if there was none).
DECLARE Appointment HAS
    `office`                                              IS AN Office
    `appointee`                                           IS A Person
    `made on`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `term starts on`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `made by the Governor-General`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous appointment to the office was made on`  IS A NUMBER
    `Selection Committees for the office`                 IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
    `the Minister is satisfied the appointee has no significant political affiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Senate passed a resolution approving it`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Senate's resolution was passed on`               IS A NUMBER
    `the House passed a resolution approving it`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the House's resolution was passed on`                IS A NUMBER
    `a statement of reasons was tabled in the Senate`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Senate statement was tabled on`                  IS A NUMBER
    `a statement of reasons was tabled in the House`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the House statement was tabled on`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 11(1)(a), (b): the occasions on which a person may act in a designated diplomatic office.
DECLARE Occasion IS ONE OF
    `a vacancy in the office`
    `the appointee is absent from duty`
    `the appointee is unable to perform the duties of the office`
    `none of these`

-- An arrangement for a person to act in an office (s 11, s 14(4)-(6)). The Bill does not say
-- who makes it or how (REF-25); the arrangement, its day and its occasion are facts.
DECLARE `acting arrangement` HAS
    `office`                                    IS AN Office
    `the chargé d’affaires`                     IS A Person
    `made on`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `occasion`                                  IS AN Occasion
    `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Which Committees count for an appointment`

-- FORK-04, reading A (taken): "a Selection Committee established for the purpose of making such a
-- recommendation" (s 9(3)(a), (b)) and "that particular appointment" (s 10(6)) mean a Committee
-- established for the current vacancy, that is, after the previous appointment to the office was
-- made. s 10(7) ("a Selection Committee's recommendation ... is of no effect after an appointment
-- to the office is made") and the s 10(7) note ("historical recommendations cannot be relied on
-- for subsequent appointments") point the same way.
@ref s 9(3)(a), (b); s 10(6), (7)
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
`the Committees established after` p `among` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN cs
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   c's `established on` GREATER THAN p
        THEN c FOLLOWED BY `the Committees established after` p `among` rest
        ELSE `the Committees established after` p `among` rest

GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
`the Committees for this appointment` a MEANS
    `the Committees established after` (a's `the previous appointment to the office was made on`) `among` (a's `Selection Committees for the office`)

-- FORK-04, reading B: every Committee ever established for an appointment to the office counts.
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
`the Committees for this appointment, reading B` a MEANS
    a's `Selection Committees for the office`

§ `10 Recommendations by Selection Committees`

§§ `The list`

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of candidates on` es MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS `the number of candidates on` rest

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of candidates on` es `with a significant political affiliation on` r MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF `has a significant political affiliation on` (e's `candidate`) r THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number of candidates on` rest `with a significant political affiliation on` r

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a candidate on` es `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` r MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` (e's `candidate`) r
     OR `a candidate on` rest `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` r

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every candidate on` es `with a significant political affiliation on` r `has reasons set out` MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        ((NOT (`has a significant political affiliation on` (e's `candidate`) r)) OR e's `the list sets out reasons despite the affiliation`)
        AND `every candidate on` rest `with a significant political affiliation on` r `has reasons set out`

GIVEN n IS A STRING, es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the candidate named` n `is on` es MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (e's `candidate`'s `name` EQUALS n) OR `the candidate named` n `is on` rest

§§ `10(1) and (6) Candidate list: when, and how many`

-- s 10(6): "If: (a) a Selection Committee established for an appointment to a designated
-- diplomatic office refers the matter back to the Minister; and (b) the Minister subsequently
-- establishes another Selection Committee (the second or subsequent Committee) for that
-- particular appointment; subsection (1) has effect in relation to the second or subsequent
-- Committee as if the reference to a list of between 2 and 10 (inclusive) proposed candidates
-- were instead a reference to a list of 2 or 3 proposed candidates."
-- `earlier` are the Committees for the same appointment (FORK-04 decides which those are; the list
-- may include c and later Committees: only those established before c are read). c is second or
-- subsequent if one of them referred the matter back on or before the day c was established.
@ref s 10(6)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, earlier IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `is a second or subsequent Committee after` earlier IF
    CONSIDER earlier
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (    x's `established on` LESS THAN c's `established on`
         AND `the Committee referred the matter back` x
         AND x's `notice given on` AT MOST c's `established on`)
     OR `the Committee` c `is a second or subsequent Committee after` rest

-- s 10(1): "The Minister must, within 7 days of establishing a Selection Committee for an
-- appointment to a designated diplomatic office, give the Selection Committee a list of between
-- 2 and 10 (inclusive) proposed candidates for the appointment."
@ref s 10(1), (6)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, earlier IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the list for` c `after` earlier `has a permitted number of candidates` IF
    IF   `the Committee` c `is a second or subsequent Committee after` earlier
    THEN n AT LEAST 2 AND n AT MOST 3
    ELSE n AT LEAST 2 AND n AT MOST 10
    WHERE
        n MEANS `the number of candidates on` (c's `list`)

-- "within 7 days of establishing": FORK-05, reading A (taken): the 7 days begin on the day after
-- the day of establishment (the day of the event is excluded: Acts Interpretation Act s 36(1),
-- items 5 and 6, by analogy), so the last day is the 7th day after it; then s 36(2) carries a last
-- day that is a Saturday, Sunday or holiday to the next day that is none of those.
@ref s 10(1); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1), (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for giving the list to` c `in` w MEANS
    `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is`
        (`the first day of a period beginning after` (c's `established on`) PLUS 6)
        `and the holidays are` (w's `holidays`)

-- FORK-05, reading B: the 7 days include the day of establishment, so the last day is the 6th day
-- after it (then s 36(2)).
@ref s 10(1); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1) item 2, (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for giving the list, reading B, to` c `in` w MEANS
    `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is`
        (`the first day of a period beginning on` (c's `established on`) PLUS 6)
        `and the holidays are` (w's `holidays`)

@ref s 10(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the list was given to` c `in time in` w IF
        c's `list given`
    AND c's `list given on` AT LEAST c's `established on`
    AND c's `list given on` AT MOST `the last day for giving the list to` c `in` w

@ref s 10(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the list was given to` c `in time, reading B, in` w IF
        c's `list given`
    AND c's `list given on` AT LEAST c's `established on`
    AND c's `list given on` AT MOST `the last day for giving the list, reading B, to` c `in` w

§§ `10(2) What the list may propose`

-- s 10(2): "The list: (a) must not propose any candidate who has a disqualifying political
-- affiliation; and (b) if the list proposes between 2 and 4 candidates (inclusive)--may only
-- propose 1 candidate who has a significant political affiliation; and (c) if the list proposes
-- between 5 and 10 candidates (inclusive)--may only propose up to 2 candidates who have a
-- significant political affiliation; and (d) for each candidate who has a significant political
-- affiliation (if any)--must set out reasons why the candidate would be appropriate for
-- appointment to the office despite the candidate's significant political affiliation."
-- Affiliations are tested on the day the list is given (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-06).
@ref s 10(2)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(2)(a) is met by the list for` c IF
    (NOT `a candidate on` (c's `list`) `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` (c's `list given on`))

@ref s 10(2)(b), (c)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(2)(b) and (c) are met by the list for` c IF
    BRANCH
        IF n AT LEAST 2 AND n AT MOST 4  THEN spa AT MOST 1
        IF n AT LEAST 5 AND n AT MOST 10 THEN spa AT MOST 2
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        n   MEANS `the number of candidates on` (c's `list`)
        spa MEANS `the number of candidates on` (c's `list`) `with a significant political affiliation on` (c's `list given on`)

@ref s 10(2)(d)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(2)(d) is met by the list for` c IF
    `every candidate on` (c's `list`) `with a significant political affiliation on` (c's `list given on`) `has reasons set out`

-- s 10(1) and (2) together: the Minister's duties about the list.
@ref s 10(1), (2), (6)
GIVEN c       IS A `Selection Committee`
      earlier IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      w       IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister complied with s 10(1) and (2) for` c `after` earlier `in` w IF
        `the list was given to` c `in time in` w
    AND `the list for` c `after` earlier `has a permitted number of candidates`
    AND `s 10(2)(a) is met by the list for` c
    AND `s 10(2)(b) and (c) are met by the list for` c
    AND `s 10(2)(d) is met by the list for` c

§§ `10(3) to (5) The Committee's decision`

-- s 10(3): "The Selection Committee must, within 2 months after receiving the list, give the
-- Minister a written notice: (a) if the Selection Committee agrees on a candidate for the
-- appointment--recommending the candidate's appointment to the office; or (b) otherwise--referring
-- the matter back to the Minister."
-- "within 2 months after receiving the list": the period begins after the day of receipt (Acts
-- Interpretation Act s 36(1), item 6), runs 2 months under s 2G(2), and s 36(2) carries a last
-- day that is a Saturday, Sunday or holiday forward. The list is taken to be received on the day
-- it is given (REF-24; ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-13).
@ref s 10(3); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ss 2G(2), 36(1) item 6, 36(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for the Committee's notice for` c `in` w MEANS
    `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is`
        (`the last day of a period of` 2 `months starting on` (`the first day of a period beginning after` (c's `list given on`)))
        `and the holidays are` (w's `holidays`)

@ref s 10(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `gave its notice in time in` w IF
        c's `list given`
    AND c's `notice given`
    AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST `the last day for the Committee's notice for` c `in` w

-- "if the Selection Committee agrees on a candidate": FORK-08, reading A (taken): the Committee
-- agrees when the question of recommending the candidate is carried under s 13(3) at a quorate
-- meeting (s 13(1), (2)). FORK-06, reading A (taken): "a candidate for the appointment" is a
-- candidate on the list the Minister gave.
@ref s 10(3)(a); s 13(1)-(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `agrees on the candidate named` n IF
        `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c
    AND `the question was carried` c
    AND `the candidate named` n `is on` (c's `list`)

-- FORK-08, reading B: "agrees" means all three members agree.
@ref s 10(3)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `agrees, reading B of FORK-08, on the candidate named` n IF
        `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c
    AND c's `votes for` AT LEAST 3
    AND `the candidate named` n `is on` (c's `list`)

-- FORK-06, reading B: the Committee may agree on a person who was not on the list (s 10(4) lets it
-- inform itself from anyone).
@ref s 10(3)(a), (4)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `agrees, reading B of FORK-06, on the candidate named` n IF
        `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c
    AND `the question was carried` c

-- FORK-07, reading B (majority of votes cast) at the level of s 10(3)(a).
@ref s 10(3)(a); s 13(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `agrees, reading B of FORK-07, on the candidate named` n IF
        `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c
    AND `the question was carried, reading B` c
    AND `the candidate named` n `is on` (c's `list`)

-- s 10(3)(a): the Committee recommends the candidate named n when it gives a written notice
-- recommending that candidate and it agreed on that candidate.
@ref s 10(3)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `recommends the candidate named` n IF
        c's `notice given`
    AND (CONSIDER c's `notice`
         WHEN `recommending` m THEN m EQUALS n
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `the Committee` c `agrees on the candidate named` n

-- The Committee recommends someone.
@ref s 10(3)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee made a recommendation` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `notice`
    WHEN `recommending` m THEN `the Committee` c `recommends the candidate named` m
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 10(3)(b): "otherwise--referring the matter back to the Minister". A referral is a decision
-- under s 10(3), so s 13(1) requires it to be made at a meeting, and s 13(2) a quorate one
-- (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-15: no majority is required for it, since it is what follows when the
-- Committee does not agree).
@ref s 10(3)(b); s 13(1), (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee referred the matter back` c IF
        c's `notice given`
    AND (CONSIDER c's `notice`
         WHEN `referring the matter back to the Minister` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c

-- s 10(4): "The Selection Committee may, in making a decision for the purposes of subsection (3),
-- seek assistance, input or information from such persons as the Selection Committee determines."
-- A permission with no condition; nothing to decide.

-- s 10(5) (dissolution) is encoded in part3-committees.l4 with s 12(8), which it limits.

§§ `10(7) Recommendations apply only to particular vacancies`

-- s 10(7): "To avoid doubt, a Selection Committee's recommendation for an appointment to a
-- designated diplomatic office is of no effect after an appointment to the office is made."
-- A recommendation has effect on day d if it was given on or before d and no appointment to the
-- office was made after it and before d. `p` is the day of the last appointment to the office made
-- before d.
@ref s 10(7)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, d IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recommendation of` c `has effect on` d `when the last appointment before it was made on` p IF
        `the Committee made a recommendation` c
    AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST d
    AND c's `notice given on` GREATER THAN p

§ `9 Appointments to designated diplomatic offices`

§§ `9(2) Appointments when a Selection Committee makes a recommendation`

GIVEN n IS A STRING, p IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Committee recommends` n `with effect, after` p `, on` d `among` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (`the Committee` c `recommends the candidate named` n AND `the recommendation of` c `has effect on` d `when the last appointment before it was made on` p)
     OR `a Committee recommends` n `with effect, after` p `, on` d `among` rest

-- s 9(2): "This subsection applies if a Selection Committee recommends the person's appointment to
-- the office." Read with s 10(7): the recommendation must still have effect when the appointment
-- is made.
@ref s 9(2); s 10(7)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(2) applies to` a IF
    `a Committee recommends` (a's `appointee`'s `name`) `with effect, after` (a's `the previous appointment to the office was made on`) `, on` (a's `made on`) `among` (a's `Selection Committees for the office`)

-- FORK-09, reading A (taken): s 9(2) permits an appointment of the recommended person; nothing in
-- the operative provisions obliges the Minister, or anyone, to make it. The simplified outline
-- (s 3: "any person so recommended by the Selection Committee must be appointed") and EM para 18
-- say otherwise; s 3 is not operative (coverage.json).
@ref s 9(1), (2); s 3
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `someone must appoint the person a Committee recommended for` a IF FALSE

-- FORK-09, reading B: the person a Committee recommends must be appointed.
@ref s 3; s 9(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `someone must appoint the person a Committee recommended, reading B, for` a IF
    `section 9(2) applies to` a

§§ `9(3) Appointments when no recommendation from a Selection Committee`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Committee had made a recommendation by` d `among` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (`the Committee made a recommendation` c AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST d)
     OR `a Committee had made a recommendation by` d `among` rest

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of Committees that had referred the matter back by` d `among` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF `the Committee referred the matter back` c AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST d THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number of Committees that had referred the matter back by` d `among` rest

-- s 9(3)(a): "no recommendation for an appointment to the office has been made by a Selection
-- Committee established for the purpose of making such a recommendation"; (b): "at least two such
-- Selection Committees have instead referred the matter back to the Minister".
-- FORK-04, reading A (taken): the Committees for this appointment (this vacancy).
@ref s 9(3)(a), (b)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraphs 9(3)(a) and (b) are met for` a IF
        (NOT `a Committee had made a recommendation by` (a's `made on`) `among` (`the Committees for this appointment` a))
    AND `the number of Committees that had referred the matter back by` (a's `made on`) `among` (`the Committees for this appointment` a) AT LEAST 2

-- FORK-04, reading B: every Committee ever established for an appointment to the office.
@ref s 9(3)(a), (b)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraphs 9(3)(a) and (b) are met, reading B of FORK-04, for` a IF
        (NOT `a Committee had made a recommendation by` (a's `made on`) `among` (`the Committees for this appointment, reading B` a))
    AND `the number of Committees that had referred the matter back by` (a's `made on`) `among` (`the Committees for this appointment, reading B` a) AT LEAST 2

-- s 9(3)(c)(i): "the Minister is satisfied the person does not have a significant political
-- affiliation". FORK-10, reading A (taken): the condition is the Minister's state of
-- satisfaction, a fact; whether the person in truth has such an affiliation does not enter it.
@ref s 9(3)(c)(i)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(i) is met for` a IF
    a's `the Minister is satisfied the appointee has no significant political affiliation`

-- FORK-10, reading B: the Minister must be satisfied, and the person must in fact have no
-- significant political affiliation on the day of the appointment.
@ref s 9(3)(c)(i); s 8(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(i) is met, reading B of FORK-10, for` a IF
        a's `the Minister is satisfied the appointee has no significant political affiliation`
    AND (NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` (a's `appointee`) (a's `made on`))

-- s 9(3)(c)(ii): "both Houses of Parliament pass a resolution approving the person's appointment
-- to the office". FORK-11, reading A (taken): both resolutions must have been passed by the day
-- the appointment is made, since s 9(1) asks whether s 9(3) applies when the person "may be
-- appointed" (EM para 19 reads it so).
@ref s 9(3)(c)(ii)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(ii) is met for` a IF
        a's `the Senate passed a resolution approving it`
    AND a's `the Senate's resolution was passed on` AT MOST a's `made on`
    AND a's `the House passed a resolution approving it`
    AND a's `the House's resolution was passed on` AT MOST a's `made on`

-- FORK-11, reading B: the resolutions may come after the appointment ("pass" in the present tense,
-- approval after the event).
@ref s 9(3)(c)(ii)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(ii) is met, reading B of FORK-11, for` a IF
        a's `the Senate passed a resolution approving it`
    AND a's `the House passed a resolution approving it`

-- s 9(3): "This subsection applies if: (a) ...; and (b) ...; and (c) either: (i) ...; or (ii) ...".
@ref s 9(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(3) applies to` a IF
        `paragraphs 9(3)(a) and (b) are met for` a
    AND (`subparagraph 9(3)(c)(i) is met for` a OR `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(ii) is met for` a)

§§ `9(1) Appointments`

-- s 9(1): "A person may be appointed to a designated diplomatic office only if: (a) the person
-- does not have a disqualifying political affiliation; and (b) subsection (2) or (3) applies."
-- The affiliation is tested on the day the appointment is made.
@ref s 9(1)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(1) permits` a IF
        (NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` (a's `appointee`) (a's `made on`))
    AND (`section 9(2) applies to` a OR `section 9(3) applies to` a)

§§ `9(4) and (5) Tabling requirement`

-- s 9(4): "If a person is appointed to a designated diplomatic office because the Minister is
-- satisfied in accordance with subparagraph (3)(c)(i), the Minister must table in each House of
-- the Parliament a statement of reasons setting out why the Minister is so satisfied."
-- FORK-12, reading A (taken): the appointment is made "because" the Minister is satisfied when it
-- rests on s 9(3) (s 9(2) does not apply) and s 9(3)(c)(i) is met, whether or not both Houses have
-- also resolved under s 9(3)(c)(ii).
@ref s 9(4)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must table a statement of reasons for` a IF
        (NOT `section 9(2) applies to` a)
    AND `paragraphs 9(3)(a) and (b) are met for` a
    AND `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(i) is met for` a

-- FORK-12, reading B: when both Houses have also approved the appointment, it is made because of
-- their resolutions, and no statement is required.
@ref s 9(4)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must table a statement of reasons, reading B of FORK-12, for` a IF
        `the Minister must table a statement of reasons for` a
    AND (NOT `subparagraph 9(3)(c)(ii) is met for` a)

-- s 9(5): "The statement must be tabled within 5 sitting days of that House after the appointment
-- is made." A sitting day is a day the House actually sits (Acts Interpretation Act s 2M).
-- FORK-13, reading A (taken): the sitting days counted are those after the day the appointment is
-- made; a sitting on the day of the appointment does not count (s 36(1), item 6, by analogy).
-- The statement is in time if it is tabled no later than the 5th such sitting day.
@ref s 9(5); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ss 2M, 36(1)
GIVEN made IS A NUMBER, tabled IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A NUMBER, sittings IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statement for an appointment made on` made `, tabled` tabled `on` t `, was in time given the sittings` sittings IF
        tabled
    AND t AT LEAST made
    AND `the number of sitting days after` made `up to and including` t `among` sittings AT MOST 5

-- FORK-13, reading B: a sitting on the day of the appointment, after it is made, counts as the
-- first of the 5.
@ref s 9(5); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2M
GIVEN made IS A NUMBER, tabled IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A NUMBER, sittings IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statement for an appointment made on` made `, tabled` tabled `on` t `, was in time, reading B, given the sittings` sittings IF
        tabled
    AND t AT LEAST made
    AND `the number of sitting days after` (made MINUS 1) `up to and including` t `among` sittings AT MOST 5

@ref s 9(4), (5)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement was tabled in time in the Senate for` a `in` w IF
    `a statement for an appointment made on` (a's `made on`) `, tabled` (a's `a statement of reasons was tabled in the Senate`) `on` (a's `the Senate statement was tabled on`) `, was in time given the sittings` (w's `Senate sitting days`)

@ref s 9(4), (5)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement was tabled in time in the House for` a `in` w IF
    `a statement for an appointment made on` (a's `made on`) `, tabled` (a's `a statement of reasons was tabled in the House`) `on` (a's `the House statement was tabled on`) `, was in time given the sittings` (w's `House of Representatives sitting days`)

-- The requirement is breached in a House by the end of day d if a statement was required, that
-- House has sat 5 times after the appointment by d, and no statement was tabled in time.
@ref s 9(4), (5)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tabling requirement for` a `in` w `is breached in the Senate by the end of` d IF
        `the Minister must table a statement of reasons for` a
    AND `the number of sitting days after` (a's `made on`) `up to and including` d `among` (w's `Senate sitting days`) AT LEAST 5
    AND (NOT (`the statement was tabled in time in the Senate for` a `in` w AND a's `the Senate statement was tabled on` AT MOST d))

@ref s 9(4), (5)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tabling requirement for` a `in` w `is breached in the House by the end of` d IF
        `the Minister must table a statement of reasons for` a
    AND `the number of sitting days after` (a's `made on`) `up to and including` d `among` (w's `House of Representatives sitting days`) AT LEAST 5
    AND (NOT (`the statement was tabled in time in the House for` a `in` w AND a's `the House statement was tabled on` AT MOST d))

§ `11 Acting arrangements for designated diplomatic offices`

-- s 11(1): "This section applies in relation to a person (the chargé d'affaires) acting in a
-- designated diplomatic office: (a) during a vacancy in the office; or (b) during any period, or
-- during all periods, when a person appointed to the office: (i) is absent from duty; or (ii) is,
-- for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office."
@ref s 11(1)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 applies to` x IF
        `is a designated diplomatic office` (x's `office`)
    AND (CONSIDER x's `occasion`
         WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 11(2): "The chargé d'affaires must not have a disqualifying political affiliation or a
-- significant political affiliation."
-- FORK-14, reading A (taken): tested when the arrangement is made, which is what s 14(4) ("must
-- not be made otherwise than in accordance with this Act") reads.
@ref s 11(2)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(2) is met for` x IF
        (NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` (x's `the chargé d’affaires`) (x's `made on`))
    AND (NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` (x's `the chargé d’affaires`) (x's `made on`))

-- FORK-14, reading B: s 11(2) is a continuing requirement, tested on each day d of the acting.
@ref s 11(2)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(2) is met, reading B of FORK-14, for` x `on` d IF
        (NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` (x's `the chargé d’affaires`) d)
    AND (NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` (x's `the chargé d’affaires`) d)

-- s 11(3): "To avoid doubt, this section applies to the chargé d'affaires instead of section 9."
@ref s 11(3)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 applies to the chargé d'affaires under` x IF
    FALSE
